    ("the six-site rotor's skew (MODEL, 15:04)", "S = R - R^T has rank 4 and is killed by S^4 + 5S^2 + 5I, of rank 2; the five powers of R add to it", "replayed: t^2 - 5t + 5 in t = -S^2, the relation of the golden pairs 2 + phi and 3 - phi; the sum of the powers is 5 P_fix; the windings R - R^4 and R^2 - R^3 have Gram 10I", T, "23"),
    ("Karma's commutators (MODEL, 15:04)", "K^2 = -4I, and [K, B^n] has trace 0 and determinant -29 F_n^2 through the tenth", "replayed with a witness K = [[1, 1], [-5, -1]]: [K, B^n] = F_n [K, B] for every n; 29 = h - 1 is the highest root's marks without the leading 1; the sibling's operand is not stored here", T, "23"),
    ("the Names' clock readings (MODEL, 14:49)", "540 of order 8; 11 and 29 generate; 108 = 3 mod 5; the yugas add to 4320; x3 kills the nakshatra seam; 736 of order 135; 3600 of order 6; the golden landings 0, 216, 864, 1080, 0", "replayed; readings, not joins", T, "23"),
    ("doubling after a triple translation (MODEL, 15:04)", "on <864>, doubling after a triple translation equals two translations", "corrected: 2(x + 3) = 2x + 1 mod 5, one translation after doubling; two translations after doubling is doubling after one", T, "23"),
    ("the Gauss operator as a polynomial in the skew (separate model, 15:32)", "S^4 + 5S^2 + 5I = 5 P_fix, G = -2S^2 - 5 P_moving, G^2 = 5 P_moving on the source rotor", "replayed on the six-site rotor and on the five sites, where G5 = -2S^2 - 5I + J: the pentagon operator is a polynomial in the rotor's skew part and the moving projector; the separate model's stored source and frame matrices satisfy the same identities (its source skew is metric-skew, not skew as a matrix)", T, "23"),
    ("the cyclic maps (separate model, 15:43)", "on Z/n multiplication by m has kernel <n/g> and image <g>, g = gcd(n, m); on Z/4320 the kernel of x9 is <480>, its image <9> the kernel of x mod 9, and the kernel of x3 their meet {0, 1440, 2880}", "replayed for every multiplier m on Z/4320", T, "23"),
    ("the publication pointer at N34 (hub, 15:21)", "CURRENT_RELEASE names N34: 3755 and 3710 sheets, four copies verified; the lag at N33 that the sibling and the separate model noted is closed", "recorded; the intake arithmetic 76 + 2 + 2 + 3 = 83 and 4 + 6 + 3 + 3 = 16 holds", T, "23"),
    ("the matched generator's readings (MODEL, 15:30)", "source diagonal 2367/10, off-diagonal scale 47/20, innovation ratio -4909/188, gains 2 and -3 differing by 5", "replayed as arithmetic: 2367/10 = 232 + 47/10, 47/20 is half of 47/10, 188 = 4 x 47 with 47 the moment-gap integer; the two-reading inverse [[g1, 1], [g2, 1]]^-1 needs g1 != g2; the generator is not stored here", T, "23"),
    ("the five-cycle's doubling (MODEL, 09:36)", "x -> 2x on the five sites has order 4, conjugates R to R^2 and G5 to -G5, and its square conjugates S to -S", "replayed with S^4 + 5S^2 + 5I = J, G5^2 = 5I - J and G5 + G5^2 + 2S^2 = 0 on the five sites; it is the doubling of the tick Z/5 acting on the sites", T, "23"),
    ("the separate model's stored matrices (MODEL, 09:36)", "the stored source skew's quartic S^4 + 5S^2 + 5I has rank 1 and trace 5 and adds with the stored Gauss square to 5I; the frame skew's quartic has rank 2 and trace 10; the exterior pulse cleared of 5 squares to 5 times itself", "replayed as data on the stored entries: the quartics over 5 are projectors of trace 1 and 2, the frame skew kills its quartic, the stored Gauss square has rank 4 and trace 20 and is not 5I - J, and the stored map into A4 is 4 x 5 of rank 4", T, "23"),
    ("the cyclic maps linearized (MODEL, 09:36)", "as 0/1 matrices on Q^4320, x -> 9x has rank 480 and nullity 3840 and x -> x mod 9 has rank 9 and nullity 4311; neither nullity is the group kernel", "replayed with numpy ranks: the linear ranks are the image counts 480 and 9 and both group kernels are <480>, of order 9; the orders 3840 -> 9, 9 -> 480, 4311 -> 480, 480 -> 9 hold and the nine preimages of 18 are 2 + 480k", T, "23"),
    ("the Quotient's receipt readings (MODEL, 09:36)", "630 has order 48; 633, 21 and 3 have order 1440; 4176 has order 30; 37 generates the circle; 43200 = 10 x 4320 is 0 on it", "replayed as arithmetic; the receipts' groups and regressions are recorded, not rerun", T, "23"),
    ("the Label's selected diagonal (MODEL, 09:36)", "Y = diag(0, 2, 2, 2, -3, -3) has minimal polynomial t(t - 2)(t + 3), Vandermonde 30 and discriminant 900 = 6 x 10 x 15; the cleared projectors have ranks 1, 3, 2 and 5 x 6P0 + 3 x 10P2 + 2 x 15P-3 = 30I", "replayed; the Lagrange denominator at 0 is -6, so the cleared projector 6 P0 is (2I - Y)(Y + 3I), with 10 P2 = Y(Y + 3I) and 15 P-3 = Y(Y - 2I); Y - 2I has rank 3 and is not 10 P2", T, "23"),
    ("the Label's hook lengths (MODEL, 09:36)", "S7's hook lengths give 1, 6, 20, 15 for [7], [6, 1], [4, 1, 1, 1], [5, 1, 1]; 100(1 + 6) = 700 = 20(20 + 15) = 20 x 35 with 35 = C(7, 3); 700 has order 216 and 600 order 36; 719 generates the circle", "replayed as arithmetic; 700, 800 and 900 miss the tick and 7, 8, 9 meet it; the ordinary and parity readings, the 719-dimensional kernel and the equivariant Hom are not stored here", T, "23"),
    ("the paired readout (MODEL, 10:05)", "the three disjoint pair swaps R (one involution) and the probe Q = diag(1, -1, 1, -1, 1, -1) anticommute; O O^T = 2I and O^T O = I + R for the sum readout O; the stack [O; OQ] has M^T M = 2I, determinant 8 and mod-2 rank 3; the correlation x1 x2 + x3 x4 + x5 x6 = (|Ox|^2 - |OQx|^2)/4 is kept by R and reversed by Q", "replayed on the separate model's stored swap, probe, sum and two-view matrices; ker O is the odd space, so three further readings are necessary and the difference readout supplies them", T, "23"),
    ("the literal weights 700, 7, 800, 8, 900, 9 (MODEL, 10:05)", "the swap defect D - RDR is 99 diag(7, -7, 8, -8, 9, -9), of rank 6, the even part D + RDR is 101 diag(7, 7, 8, 8, 9, 9), and the weighted stack [O; OD] has determinant 693 x 792 x 891", "replayed; 99 meets the tick and 100 does not; the weighted stack inverts over Q pair by pair", T, "23"),
    ("the pair swap against the six-site rotor (MODEL, 10:05)", "TX = XR has a six-dimensional solution space; every solution factors through the rank-2 fixed projector of T and the rank-3 even projector of R and has rank at most 2, so no invertible equivariant adapter exists", "replayed on the model's rotor T (order 5, fixing x0): nullity 6, a rank-2 witness, the identity not a solution; the separate model's stored rank-2 adapter intertwines R with T conjugated by the site swap (0 3), a five-cycle fixing site 3 as the separate model's frame rotor does, not with T itself", T, "23"),
    ("the four-coordinate reader (seven-code court, 09:38)", "on the ordered family (600, 009, 800, 008) the stack [O4; O4 Q4] has determinant -4 and inverts to the stored decoder; z1 z3 + z2 z4 = (s1 s2 + d1 d2)/2 and z1 z4 + z2 z3 = (s1 s2 - d1 d2)/2; no rank-2 observer determines a nondegenerate quadratic", "replayed; the lag-two form has determinant 1/16 and its bilinear form does not vanish on the kernel of O4", T, "23"),
    ("the 700 obstruction (seven-code court, 09:38)", "with S7 permuting seven sites and acting trivially on the auxiliary factors, Hom_S7(V7 (x) 1_100, 1_20 (x) Lambda^3 V7) = 0 although both have dimension 700; a transposition has characters 500 and 100 on them", "replayed over all 5040 permutations: <chi_V, chi_3> = 0, <chi_V, chi_V> = <chi_3, chi_3> = 2, and Lambda^2 V7 shares one constituent with each; the Label note's missing actions are supplied by the court", T, "23"),
    ("the selected diagonal's resolution (seven-code court, 09:38; the readout and seven-code archives)", "Y^2 + Y - 6I = -6 P0, tr Y^2 = 30 and Y = (10 P2 - 15 P-3)/5; the characteristic polynomial t (t - 2)^3 (t + 3)^2 has discriminant 0 while the minimal polynomial's is 900", "replayed; the archives' stored N0, N2, N-3 are the cleared projectors 6 P0, 10 P2, 15 P-3 of the 09:37 check", T, "23"),
    ("the smear and Markov helpers (seven-code court, 09:38)", "ker(S Delta) = ker Delta for an invertible S, and the similarity B' = SB, D' = S D S^-1, C' = C S^-1 keeps every Markov parameter C D^n B", "replayed on integer witnesses through order 8", T, "23"),
    ("the typed adapter's chart (separate model, 10:43)", "the stored rank-2 adapter intertwines its declared Golden-frame rotor exactly and fails by a rank-2 residual against an older rotor given without a chart; the intertwiners form a six-dimensional space, not a six-element set", "replayed: the declared rotor is the model's six-site rotor conjugated by a site permutation (five of them do it, none the swap (0 3) of the 10:05 row, whose conjugate the adapter also intertwines since AR = A); the older rotor is similar over Q to both (the maps X with X A6 = T_d X form a space of dimension 8 = 4 + 4 with invertible members S), and the transported adapter S^-1 A intertwines it with the swap, so the defect is a missing chart, not a missing adapter", T, "23"),
    ("the icosian folding (the 12:50 synthesis, 31 Oct; the quasicrystal row)", "E8 -> H4 + phi H4 icosian folding, attributed by the document to arXiv:2605.15075 (identified by search as 'Non-crystallographic systems of integers over composition algebras', 2026, not read: arxiv.org is unreachable here; its own 240-element H4 + H4 shell belongs to a rank-16 order, not to E8; the folding is classical)", "replayed from the 120 unit icosians, not from the paper: under the twisted trace form 2 Tr(alpha Re(p qbar)), alpha = phi/sqrt5 of norm 1/disc Q(sqrt5), the icosian ring is E8 with an explicit isometry from the model's roots; the 240 roots are the 120 units and the 120 phi^-1 units, the document's 'H4 + phi H4' being the same two scales in the other real embedding, which the day exchanges; the tick is left multiplication by an order-5 unit, the golden companion is multiplication by phi, and W(H4) = C_W(X) has 14400 elements and holds c' as a Coxeter element of H4 (icosians)", T, "23"),
    ("the tick's SL(2,5) (layer 25, revisited)", "C_W(g) acts on the residue plane F25 as SL(2,5), the binary icosahedral group, and on the six lines as the icosahedron on its six axes", "the SL(2,5) is the right multiplication by the 120 unit icosians on I/(1 - u)I = F25, C_W(g) = (Z/10 x 2I)/{+-1} is left multiplication by +-u^k times right multiplication by units, and the six lines are the six Sylow 5-subgroups of 2I, the axes of the icosahedron whose vertices are the imaginary parts of the twelve order-5 units of trace phi^-1 (icosians)", T, "23, 25"),
    ("the Penrose planes (the 12:50 synthesis, 31 Oct; the quasicrystal row)", "A4 -> Penrose tiling, as far as the scheme: (E1, E2, A4) with injective and dense projections and the Galois star map; attributed by the document to arXiv:2604.10574 ('Tiles from projections of the root and weight lattices of A_n', 2026, which restates it as background; the result is de Bruijn 1981 and Baake, Kramer, Schlottmann and Zeidler 1990)", "built exactly over Q(sqrt5): the five-cycle splits A4 (x) R into two Galois-conjugate golden planes, the roots project as two decagons at radii in the ratio phi, the projection is injective on A4 with dense image (Kronecker cited), the scheme has the Galois conjugation as its star map and A4*/A4 = Z/5 as the four vertex classes; the Penrose vertex sets as unions of four of its model sets, their windows and the tiling are cited, not replayed (penrose_planes)", T, "23"),
    ("the index-5 A4 + A4 (the 12:50 synthesis, 31 Oct; the quasicrystal row)", "index-5 A4 + A4 in E8, attributed by the document to arXiv:1903.10851 ('Quantum Gravity at the Fifth Root of Unity', spin foams at a fifth root of unity, which never mentions A4 or sublattices of E8)", "already held: layer 11's glue and layer 25's six A4 + A4 from the six F5-lines; the paper's Fibonacci fusion matrix is the golden companion B as a shared matrix, not a join", T, "11, 23"),
    ("the K5 septuple and the F20 descent (the 12:50 synthesis, 31 Oct; section 2)", "C(n, 2) = 2n only at n = 5; M M^T = 3I + J, M^T M = I + J - A_Petersen; spec D^2 = {0^5, 3^8, 8^2}; G5^2 = 5I - J, M M^T + G5^2 = 8I; G^2 = 5G; R = 3I - U - U^-1 with spec {1^3, (4 - phi)^6, (3 + phi)^6}, det 11^6 and F20 average P + (7/2)(I - P); det 155, 31, 5; the address-time bijection and D T = T^2 D on Z36; the CRT idempotents (3456, 3105, 2080)", "replayed on the carrier's incidences, the signed edge tick and the five-cycle on K5's 15 = 5 + 10 (notes_1250); R is the monograph's Golden15 stiffness already held (notes_2033, the 20:33 check), realised on the carrier's atoms with the hub's R15 polynomial (t - 1)^3 (t^2 - 7t + 11)^6, the hub's operator itself still not stored here; the twenty affine maps, the twisted doubling D T = T^2 D and the idempotents already held (clock_joins, the shift-and-doubling and primary-split rows); new: on the 12-dimensional moving part X = -(U + U^-1) is the golden companion and the doubling is its Galois conjugation", T, "23"),
    ("the E8 overlattice readings (the 12:50 synthesis, 31 Oct; section 2)", "eight-root frame Gram I + J, 8/9; glue partition 240 = 20 + 20 + 4 x 50 with 32 + 8; five fourth-moment shells; root-graph spectrum and returns; lattice walks W_0..W_6; 7-design (60, 36, 30), degree-8 anisotropy 33 vs 123/4; nine frequencies F2-rank 8; half-periods 16 + 48 x 5 and 1 + 51 = 52; witness 220.6345317313; six-port 241I - J, 183I + 52J, 171; port metric {2, 5 -+ sqrt5, 2/5}; mixing 32 sqrt5/675", "replayed from glue.roots() by exact convolution of root steps and exact moment tensors (notes_1250); corrected: the degree-8 moments are 57/2 at e1 and 39 at (e1 + e2)/sqrt2, not 33 and 123/4 (the anisotropy stands, the two values do not); read as: the glue class sums the five A4(1) coordinates, as 'relative to A4(1) + A4(2)' says, and over all eight the formula would give 126, 56, 56, 1, 1; the variance 171 is MEMORY's stated block (stated_block, golden_root_port); the partition, the root-graph spectrum and the walk counts already held (the L0, six-line quotient and two-walk-counts rows)", T, "23"),
    ("the open computations (the 12:50 synthesis, 31 Oct; section 4)", "walk recurrence past order 6, channel densities, collar positivity on (220.63, 224), bath memory growth, resolvent matching, external operands", "recorded as open: no operand here; the collar witness itself replays (eps 220.6345317313, least tangent eigenvalue 6.985582)", RP, "23"),
    ("the Rosebud bank (hub, 30 Oct, filed 31 Oct 17:50)", "the mirror-even leaf e_23 read through the six Sylow petals of Lambda^2 A4 is a 6 x 6 bank of determinant 4/125 intertwining the mirror (01) with the opposite-petal half-turn; mirror-even and mirror-odd 3 x 3 decoders (det -1/5, -2/25; inverse norms 3, 6; ||B^-1|| = 7); a mirror-even leaf (0, a, b, a, b, c) reconstructs iff P+ P- != 0", "replayed exactly, including the hub's integer matrix 5B and both decoder inverses; the petals are ordered H_(i+1) = g H_i g^-1 from the tick's own Sylow group (notes_1751)", T, "23"),
    ("the positional flower and the record packet (hub, 30 Oct)", "C = I + W has the alternating dark stripe; the opposite-petal leaf q = e_0 - e_3 repairs it (rank 6, determinant -2, parity-intertwining); C (x) B rank 30 and [C; q] (x) B rank 36; C^T C + (CD)^T (CD) = 4I; the packet [I6; 1; 1..6] is an [8, 6, 3] MDS code; a co-rotating scan reads rank 2", "replayed exactly; the code repairs stored records only and adds no upstream information, as the note says (notes_1751)", T, "23"),
    ("the Golden measurement channel (hub's deep join, 30 Oct)", "E_i = F_i/2, sigma_j = (11I - 5F_j)/56 give tr(E_i sigma_j) = (10J - 4I)/56, the E8 six-line chain; rank 6, kernel 30; Hom_S5(L6, six labels) = 0, so the bridge is quadratic; petal-plane sources read (1/2, 1/10, ..., 1/10) on a whole circle; pair and triple petal sums have the stated characteristic polynomials and probability bounds", "replayed exactly and joined: rotor -> root graph (notes_1751); the one-step chain has no real generator and the two-step one is exp(log 196 (J/6 - I)), as already in six_lines", T, "23"),
    ("the hexad clock (hub's deep join, 30 Oct)", "D = [[1, 4], [1, 2]] over F5 with D^2 = 3R; j -> j + 144 cannot be carried through j mod 36 alone; the selected schedule f(j) = D^floor((j mod 4320)/72) line0 covers the six lines 720 times each and needs b mod 12 for j = a + 36b", "replayed: R moves every line, the schedule is equivariant at +72, +144 and +216 on all 4320 ticks and has no shorter period in b; D itself was already in notes_2356 as a selection", SR, "23"),
    ("TENET on the cycles (hub, 30 Oct)", "U = Lambda^2 rho(i -> i + 1), D = Lambda^2 rho(i -> 2i): K = 3I - U - U^-1 is G-positive with characteristic polynomial (lam - 1)^2 (lam^2 - 7 lam + 11)^2; T = diag(R, -R), R = D^2, reverses the phase flow anti-symplectically; G- = G6 (I - 2P-) has signature (5, 1), kept by R and carried by D to G+; the selected observer [PF, 0] sees rank 4 of 12; a flavour witness has tr([Hu, Hd]^3) = -12i", "replayed exactly; the temporal-pincer statement (both time directions see the same kernel for a bounded generator) is the analytic Taylor argument, cited; entropy and retrocausality claims are not mathematics of the model and are not adopted (notes_1751)", T, "23"),
    ("the filtered static locality (hub's PROOF_NOTE, 30 Oct)", "61526 G1(s) = 248 - s + s^2 G0(s); G1(0) = 124/30763; the Newton polytope of H^n T* widens by 100 per filter in scale-five units (960 -> 22080 sites); low-energy and heat constants of the first filter from the zeroth by m2 and Gamma", "replayed: the polynomial division identities through n = 5 and the stated constants; the site counts 960 and 22080 = 23 x 960 were already held; the polytope growth is Minkowski additivity (cited) (notes_1751)", T, "23"),
    ("the eighth directional moments (separate model, 31 Oct 17:24)", "the 240 roots have moments 60, 36, 30 in every direction and 57/2, 39, 179/6, 179/6 along the axis, a root, the charge (1, 1, 1, 0, -3, 0, 0, 0) and the color (1, 1, 1, 0, ...); twice the color is carried to the charge by a root permutation", "replayed: the inner-product counts, the four eighth moments, and the Weyl equivalence of 2 color and charge (one dominant representative), which explains their equal profiles (notes_1757)", T, "23"),
    ("the dispersion bound and critical points (separate model, 31 Oct 17:57)", "sigma(k) = 30q - (3/2)q^2 + q^3/24 - P8/40320 + R, 0 <= R <= q^5/30240; critical values 224 (root half-period, index 1), 256 (axis, charge and color half-periods, Hessian -4I), 250 (the golden character)", "replayed: the remainder constant 120/10! from (k.r)^2 <= 2q and the 7-design, the five gradients, values and Hessians; 224 is layer 22's E7 + A1 saddle and 250 the tick's fixed momenta (notes_1757)", T, "22"),
    ("the canon's N36 and N37 releases (31 Oct 18:02-18:22)", "N36 adds the Level Join and Degree Moment tabs; N37 the dispersion tabs (3770 and 3725 sheets), all prior cells kept, four copies hashed; pending claims K04, X01, X02 unformed", "recorded (REPORTED): the workbooks were not opened; their new mathematics is the separate model's, replayed above", RP, "23"),
    ("the Rosebud archive refiling (hub, 31 Oct 17:25-19:48)", "about 510 files of 29-30 Oct notes, receipts and verifiers re-filed in PAGE_0003 to PAGE_0008", "backlog: the notes are read as data in later checks; this check replayed the Rosebud A4, deep-join, TENET and filtered-locality notes and the claim ledgers", RP, "23"),
    ("the N39 unified model (separate model, 31 Oct 21:08, dated 1 Nov)", "the circle maps onto Z/30 with kernel of order 144, the tick and miss images of orders 5 and 6; the seesaw -D N D^T = -S N S + alpha(S N A - A N S) + alpha^2 A N A; GL(2,5)'s 480-element order census; two integer seeds of determinants 12402 and 84492 with one reduction mod 5", "replayed: the quotient (the ticks times the misses read mod 30), the seesaw identity and the census, with AIR_801 mod 5 among its 80 elements of order 24 (notes_2122); the second seed's entries are not in the note, so only AIR_801's determinant 12402 is checked", T, "23"),
    ("the N39 source readers and metric (separate model, 31 Oct)", "the source clock P31 of order 6 and Z31 = P31 G31 of order 30 with fixed ranks 7, 7, 3; four seven-port samples of rank 25 with a blind six; T6 and T7 need one and two more scalars; H31^2 = 5P with the compatible metric T6^T G6 T6 + Q^T Gavg Q; a 3 x 4 reflection quotient of rank 3 completed with determinant -1/4", "recorded (REPORTED): the source matrices are in the separate model's zip, not opened; its own 60 rational check groups report PASS", RP, "23"),
    ("the twin-prime branch (separate model's N39; hub archive of Aug 2026)", "the weak-tail bound B_p(A) = (p A^(1/p) - A)/(p - 1) < 1 exactly when A < 1, and m2 >= 2 m1^2 - 1 for a real orthogonal shift; nineteen August notes re-filed", "outside the model: the two lemmas are elementary (1 - B_p = (u^p - p u + p - 1)/(p - 1) for u = A^(1/p), and Jensen on cos 2x = 2cos^2 x - 1); the twin-prime conjecture stays open, as the note says", RP, "23"),
    ("the canon's N38 and N39 releases (31 Oct 21:05-21:20)", "N38 hand-off and staging workbooks, N39 verified-source and canon-sync workbooks with four-copy receipts; no new matrix ID, all gates frozen", "recorded (REPORTED): workbooks not opened; their new mathematics is the separate model's, replayed above", RP, "23"),
    ("the golden clock and its return (separate model's N40, 31 Oct 21:39, dated 1 Nov)", "for the saved clock C (C^5 = I), metric G and Hodge H (H^2 = 5I): L = 2I - C - C^-1, A = (C - C^-1)/2, F, B; HB = 2L - 5B, L(L^2 - 5L + 5I) = 0; (sI + L)^-1 = [s^2 I + s(5I - L) + 5F]/[s(s^2 + 5s + 5)] = F/s + [(s + 5/2)B - HB/2]/(s^2 + 5s + 5); the Schur energy criterion for W = R6(s) G^-1", "replayed on the model's own tick on the cycles with G6 and the wedge star (notes_2154): every identity holds, with HB = 2L - 5B for the wedge orientation up to the sign of H; the energy criterion is the standard Schur complement and the source's own P31, Z31, T6, S6 stay in its zip", T, "23"),
    ("the E8 root moments through degree ten (separate model's N40)", "P2 = 60q, P4 = 36q^2, P6 = 30q^3; P8 - 30q^4 harmonic; (132/5)q^4 < P8 <= 39q^4 by two sum-of-squares certificates; 4P10 - 15qP8 + 315q^5 = 0; tenth moments 225/8, 135/2, 265/8, 265/8; the Taylor remainder 0 <= sigma - T8 <= q^5/53760, sharp", "replayed exactly on the 240 roots (notes_2154), through all 19448 degree-ten coefficients; it sharpens notes_1757's q^5/30240 by the factor 9/16; the note itself says the degree-ten identity and the lower bound were in the canon's older reports", T, "22"),
    ("the canon's N40 publication state and the archive (31 Oct 21:37-21:54)", "N40 golden-moment unification release with publication state and handover; PAGE_0013 (27 Oct notes) and the twin-prime FinalGold folders of 13 Aug", "recorded (REPORTED): release receipts not opened; the archive joins the backlog", RP, "23"),
    ("one statement (the user's synthesis, 31 Oct 22:35)", "the 240 roots are the two A4 and the fibres of one K5; 28 pairs sum to each root, orthogonal pairs fill the 2160 vectors of norm 4 and 60-degree pairs the 6720 of norm 6; Agni = 5I - G on the ten edges, Soma = Agni/5; the pentagon and pentagram Laplacians add to 5I minus the fixed sum, in the cycles where Agni acts as 5; x^2 - 5x + 5 = 0 is the cycle Laplacian and at double scale the golden band 5 -+ sqrt5", "replayed and joined (cycles -> golden, one_quadratic) with G read as the signed edge Gram B^T B (so Agni = 5 P_cycles and Soma = P_cycles); the two Laplacians also multiply to the same 5I minus the fixed sum, so on the moving part they are the quadratic's two roots; the golden band at double scale is the port metric's contrast block 4I + 2X; the residual stays 0 and AUTH stays NOT_PASS", T, "23"),
    ("the N39 counted pointer (the user's synthesis, 31 Oct 22:35)", "N39 stays the counted pointer at 3782 and 3737 sheets", "recorded (REPORTED): the N39 workbooks were not opened here; the N37 receipt counted 3770 and 3725", RP, "23"),
    ("the separate model's 30th reference layer (31 Oct 22:09)", "a two-part 38 MB archive of the unified reference model: 30 layers, 4522 artifacts, 748 relationships, 179 matrix presentations", "recorded (REPORTED): the manifest and certificate were read as data and the archive was not opened; no claim in them can be replayed without its matrices", RP, "23"),
    ("all 240 roots through the A4 clock (separate model's N41, 31 Oct 22:46, dated 1 Nov)", "the coordinate five-cycle: 20 fixed roots and 44 pentagons; L = 2I - P - P^-1 on the 240 labels with L^2 - 5L + 5B = 0, ranks 64 and 176, K^2 = 5B; the wedge feature E: E P = C6 E, rank 6, det(E E^T) = 8957952, Gram 12[tr Q_i tr Q_j + 2 tr Q_i Q_j]; E L = L6 E and the return reads down; the reflection's twisted law D6 = -(Lambda^2 R4) C6^-1; sharp bounds (57/2)q^4 <= P8 <= 39q^4 and (225/8)q^5 <= P10 <= (135/2)q^5 with the certificate (5/588)(t - 21/2)(t - 315/2)", "replayed exactly (notes_2256) and joined (E8 -> cycles); the sharp lower bound 57/2, attained along all 2160 norm-four directions, sharpens notes_2154's strict 132/5; the directional Taylor constant runs from 1/129024 to 1/53760; the note credits the sharp bounds to the canon's older reports", T, "23"),
    ("two native memory channels (separate model's N42, 31 Oct 23:21, dated 1 Nov)", "the root graph's five relations and spectrum 56, 28, 8, -2, -4 (1, 8, 35, 112, 84), five reflection orbits on pairs; the 241-point Gram (B + 4I)/64 with v* M v = 16 + sum e^(ik.alpha), so the bath's spectrum is [0, 256]; E7 = [E; 1^T] with E B = 8E + 12 tau 1^T, A7 = [[232 I6, -12 tau], [0, 184]], det K7 = 358318080, kernel 61 + 172; the centered Hodge lift commutes, the metric defect has rank 2 and vanishes on the moving four-space; E7 K(s) J7 = g_mass Pi_mass + g_quad Pi_centered; 9361 two-step sites, boundary covariance 2117 Pi_mass + 389 Pi_centered, moments (184, 35973) and (232, 54213), Hankel rank 14; Radau enclosures; no finite autonomous intertwiner in L2", "replayed exactly (notes_2327), all seven statements; the cap's Gram certificate is a one-line proof of the 256 cap the model already proves; the no-intertwiner theorem follows from the absolutely continuous port measures (free_chain); the landing in the separate model's source31 clock (Z31, T7, S7) stays in its zip", T, "23"),
    ("the separate model's 31st reference layer (23:09 release and certificate)", "a 79 MB seven-part archive: 31 mathematical layers, 924 new matrix presentations, 135 new typed relationships, no new canon matrix IDs or active summands, parameters unassigned; limits: the root-label section metric differs from the saved G6, and the selected 480-bounded pencils have terminal Rayleigh values above 256 so they are not compressions of the unchanged bath", "recorded (REPORTED): the manifest and certificate were read as data; the metric limit is checked (notes_2327: K^-1 and Kc^-1 are not multiples of G6) and the pencil limit is the 256 cap (a compression of Delta has its Rayleigh values in [0, 256]); the archive itself was not opened", RP, "23"),
    ("the 021 x 120 x FOAM quadratic court (hub, 1 Nov 00:08)", "the native six-port read at the 30 flags of K5 (F = J B C, det C = 3125, det F^T F = 5^13); Sym^2 [3, 1, 1] = [5] + [1^5] + [4, 1] + 2[3, 2] + [2, 2, 1]; the 15 squared intensities have rank 15, blind [1^5] + [3, 2]; six cross terms give rank 21, det -5^35/2^26; the witness g, h with equal squares everywhere and G-norm 125; linear repair, mean-square error [1/(5 alpha^2) - |g|_G^2]/n, Fisher 30 n alpha^2 G at 0; the 120-frame averages to 1/30; gluing d_N = (30^N + 10 6^N + 15 2^N)/120; the six-site corner 241I - J is not S5-equivariant; a Gaussian information budget min(log 30, 3 log(1 + 32 E/(705 hbar)))", "replayed exactly (notes_0030), five statements, in the model's own edge flows: the six-port is the cycle space and the 15 antipodal flag pairs are the 15 synthemes; the bath point repeats the model's obstruction Hom_A5(cycles, site6) = 0; the Gaussian information budget rests on the source's own energy bound and is recorded, not replayed", T, "23"),
    ("all-level symmetry, memory and foam (separate model's N43, 1 Nov 00:53)", "N41's six centered features fail S5 (rank-5 defect per adjacent transposition); the ten edge readings (alpha_i - alpha_j)^2 - 1/2 are the smallest S5-invariant completion, [5] + [4, 1] + [3, 2], 7 -> 11 readings, kernel 229; P8 = (2(alpha.beta)^2 - 1)/48; G11(s) = diag(g_q I10, g_m), core diag(232 I10, 184), covariance diag(389 I10, 2117); walk moments to order four, Hankel 14357066531 and 219823907, beta2 > 0; block Krylov rank 7n and 11n at every depth; variational resolvent bounds lower_n <= g <= upper_n; heat/wave Taylor enclosures; the 32 x 11 codec T with two anchors, [F, T] rank 17; the A4-to-source bridge R; 266 and (32^N + 10 8^N + 15 4^N + 94 2^N)/120; a 43-node dependency registry", "replayed exactly (notes_0101), five statements, from the model's own roots and edges; it corrects any reading of N41's wedge features as an S5 module (they are a five-cycle module) and finds the half-outflow flag reader an isometry of the cycles, det B^T B = 125 being the spanning trees of K5; the all-depth Krylov rank and the no-finite-closure theorem follow from the model's absolutely continuous port measures (free_chain); the convergence rates, the heat/wave enclosures and the registry are recorded", T, "23"),
    ("the native A4 source and FOAM completion (separate model's N44, 1 Nov 01:48)", "W: Lambda^2 ker M -> cycles by commutators, rank 6, dark kernel 4 = sign x standard, absent from the 240 roots and the 32 outcomes; six odd currents on the twenty A4 roots (Sg^T Sg = 2 Gp, relations 1, -2, 0, 2, -1, moments 1, 242, 58691, 14259954, 3470101592, core 242, variance 127); the transported Hodge Hg (Hg^2 = 5, Gp-selfadjoint, odd under transpositions); the dark four on the free orbit of (-2, -1, 0, 1, 2, 0, 0, 0) (norm 10; moments 1, 243, 59132, 14407126, 3514086413, core 243, variance 83); 21 readings on 360 sites, four memory channels; a 42-outcome codec with ten oriented vertices (minimal under S5), d_N = (42^N + 10 8^N + 35 6^N + 74 2^N)/120 = 1, 4, 33, 728; a dynamic Hodge lift; the 031/130 fixtures and a 54-node registry", "replayed exactly (notes_0204), four statements, from the model's own K5, roots and FOAM coordinates; the commutator map is the model's source port W_AS, and the six currents' channel is the triangle port's cubic sector; joined as E8 -> source; the dynamic Hodge lift, the 031/130 fixtures and the registry are recorded", T, "23"),
    ("the hub's all-dots integration (1 Nov 02:18-02:22: integration, 031/130 continuation, N41 x FOAM, FOAM x E8 clock, summary)", "W: Lambda^2 P5 -> L6 rank 6 kernel 4, three phases 30 -> 18; the D15 clock A = rho(g) x c, R = rho(t) x r; FOAM ranks 6, 12, 18 / 12, 18 / 18; MF = 0; Fisher tr I^-1 = 4/(375 n alpha^2), tr G^-1 = 8/25; d_N = 1, 11, 244, 6860 with d_(N+3) = 38 d_(N+2) - 252 d_(N+1) + 360 d_N; Sym^2 kernels 34 and 294; the CRT clock j = 2241 (j mod 160) + 2080 (j mod 27); W_0..W_6; K = F E rank 6, kernel splits 32/88/30/84; P8 from 57/2 to 39; the Golden port's four channels (variances 371, 171, 1987/10 -+ 31 sqrt5/10; Hankel 357276603, 36798947, 116537713/2 -+ 90769773 sqrt5/50); dark-repair probes; a 124-dimensional Poisson fixture; boundary entropy", "replayed exactly (notes_0258), five statements: the D15 clock joins the stages to the cycles (a stage moves the cycles exactly when it lands on the time clock), and the Golden port's four channels come from the model's five root-shell sector sequences, two of them (graph 28 and -4) newly stated; the dark-repair probes, the Poisson fixture and the entropy are N44's or recorded", T, "23"),
    ("the star at the seed (join all dots, 1 Nov)", "38 new direct checked joins from E8: one to each of the 37 dots that had none and a THEOREM one to the circle, which had only a selected reference (32 THEOREM, 1 OBSTRUCTION, 2 SELECTED_REFERENCE, 3 CONDITIONAL); with the 35 dots joined before (33 by THEOREM, the circle by a selected reference, the memory clock by an obstruction) every dot but E8 now meets the seed directly", "constructed from the 240 roots, the Weyl group, the principal torus and the residue rings (join_e8_*); an independent review revised 22 of them and rejected one (a torus realization of the memory clock, which reaches only Z/90, not its 120 states); unify.star checks the star", T, "23, 25"),
    ("the 52-outcome extension and the Plucker residual (separate model's N44 addendum, 1 Nov 12:22)", "S5 multiplicities: signal 21 = 2[5] + [4,1] + [3,2] + [3,1,1] + [2,1,1,1], quadratic 21 = [5] + [1^5] + [4,1] + 2[3,2] + [2,2,1], 42 outcomes = 4[5] + [1^5] + 3[4,1] + [2,1,1,1] + 2[3,2] + [2,2,1] + [3,1,1], residual 20 = [5] + [1^5] + 2[4,1] + [3,2] + [2,2,1]; equivariant ranks 10 (S5), 11 (A5), 21 (C5), quadratic into residual 16; one [3,2] short, supplied by the ten edge labels (52 outcomes, leftover [5] + 2[4,1]), ten minimal; the 30 x 5 Plucker matrix U with U^T U = G4/81; the sign channel of norm 10; J = h r with J^2 = -I and the icosahedral traces phi, 1 - phi", "replayed exactly from the model's carriers (notes_1222, four statements); the 30 x 5 matrix is rebuilt entry for entry (det G = 162, so the isometry is 9U); joined as kerM -> readout; the Schur sandwich b/(s + 256) <= Sigma(s) <= b/s with b = (2117, 389, 127, 83) uses the boundary variances already replayed (N42, N44)", T, "23"),
    ("the packet of 1 Nov (13:40): numbers kept apart on purpose", "rotor prefix Hankel 15930273 and Jacobi 242, 127, 25998/127, 15930273/16129; two 120-sets on F2^4 + F2^4 with the same spectrum, said to agree on 96 points; 9361 sites and squared mass 1260720; m2 = 58080 periodic against 57840 = lcm(240, 241); steps 931, 241, 541 = 1 mod 5; 22^2 = 2 and 98 of order 5 mod 241; GL(2,5) 480, SL 120, an abstract 2400; the quartic a r^2 - (40/9) r^4 with zeros r^2 = 9a/40", "replayed (notes_1340, six statements): all hold except the overlap, which is 56, not 96; the rotor prefix is the six currents' spectral measure; both quadrics are E8's half-period quadric up to isometry; the gap 240 is an identity of two measures (the straight pairs); 98 is the tick's eigenvalue over F_241; the 2400 is <g> x| GL(2,5) inside W(E8); the tick fixes no time unit (an obstruction). The quartic's zero moves with a, a DYN_BIND operand; the infrared interval, the hbar thresholds and the saddle bound are not replayed", T, "23"),
    ("the binding route (separate model, 1 Nov 14:25-15:13)", "four bath channels with Jacobi data and BB* = diag(2117, 389, 127, 83); a visible-only no-go; tau^2 = -a R1/R3 (derivatives at 0) per channel with falsifiers m_k/a^k; the finite clock exp(-ihH) of order 4320 on E8/2E8 and no rank-8 lattice automorphism of that order; generator rigidity on Lambda^2 ker M (rank 75, nullity 25) with commutants 25, 5, 2, 1; the quartic matched by g^2 = 19360/9; the 48-outcome quantum observer with six Sylow labels; the 52-outcome counts and a 52 x 43 integer encoder; and the claim that two 120-sets overlap in 96", "replayed (notes_1512, six statements, six joins), all exact, the encoder stored as data/n44_52_encoder.json; corrected: no two quadric 120-sets on F2^8 can share 96 points (their symmetric difference is the support of a quadratic form, of weight 0, 128 or 128 +- 2^(7 - h), never 48); the pair x.y, q(x) + q(y) shares 56", T, "23"),
    ("the K5 temporal join (hub, re-filed 1 Nov 17:25)", "free source q'' + 4q = 0 on two lanes: port history at frequencies 0 and 4, cubic at 2 and 6 (-15/2, -17/2, 55/2, -33/2); four samples at k pi/8 tight (diag(4, 2, 2), 2 I4), quarter periods alias; ranks 17, 19, 20 (minors 48128, 145539072; jets 6, 12, 17, 18, 19, 20, minor -74402280593927700480); F20 invariance; the shear and the energy alias -47/43 (U = -7328288/238521); the causal jet with G6 = 183 I + 52 J", "replayed (notes_1725), all exact; the three blind directions are exactly the constant SL(2) lane mixings (g alternating bilinear); the F20 invariance holds for all of S5; the causal jet is CONDITIONAL on known bath data and the selected Gram", T, "23"),
    ("the quintic dark port (hub, 30 Oct, re-filed 1 Nov 17:24)", "the two dark ports share their quartic image; the residual kills all fourth-order components, starts at a rank-4 quintic (witness det -6561 x 10^18), density E^8 and heat tau^-9 against E^7 and tau^-8; G_flat = (187/5) G_B4; m1, m2 on m2 - 455 m1 + 51410 = 0 at q = 192/187; K4 witness innovations 3945/4, 3912, 30162120/34969", "replayed (notes_1725) from the model's two dark ports: the vanishing below degree 4, the quartic rank 4 with kernel D_flat, the injective quintic and rank 8, the Gram ratio, the moment line and the innovations; the witness determinant is chart-dependent and not rerun; the infrared exponents are CONDITIONAL on the standard asymptotics and the normalization constants (1/83776, 1/2035756800000, 1/50490000) are recorded", T, "23"),
    ("the seed closure, circle side (unification survey, 1 Nov)", "which of the circle's parts the seed builds: the 27-clock, vortex and coil from the singular 3-primary points; the labelling; the stage orientation; the decad's 4320-group; Weyl elements of order 36; the memory clock on the root lines", "replayed (principal.singular_primary, stage_frame, decad_stabilizer, no_order_36; memory_not_seed): c27, vortex and coil move into the derivation; the cofactor shrinks to the 2-part 2^5; three new obstructions", T, "25"),
    ("the dark-coupling non-identification (hub, 30 Oct, re-filed 1 Nov 18:20)", "the family D(t), its moments on m2 - 455 m1 + 51410 = 0 and innovation 326 - (423/4)q - (2209/16)q^2; the K4 witness 2925/2784, 713955/649800; the record norm 106339974811663945919840 x 10^360", "replayed (notes_1931); the family's real extreme q = 192/187 at t = -1/alpha is the quartic-null port (new)", T, "23"),
    ("the F20 Plucker global join (hub, 30 Oct, re-filed 1 Nov 18:20-19:16)", "native identities W G2^-1 W^T = (10/9) P, G2 = (9/10) W^T W + (3/5) C^T C; ranks 4, 7, 9, 10 at t = 1/2; degree-5 fibres, the quintic with three real roots, the three-context collision, four-context recovery, covariance completion, t = 1 blind source", "replayed (notes_1931) with the model's own mixers (the hub's are their negatives), all exact, the hub's quintic reproduced verbatim", T, "23"),
