    ("the canon snapshots THREE_LAYER_UNIFICATION and FULL_JOIN (1 Nov 21:27, 21:37)", "Hankel law 125 d^2 f (8000, 2000, 54000, 16000, 4000, 0), root golden multiplicities 64/88/88, c'^6, cycle Laplacian identity, golden Petersen K, non-identifications", "replayed (notes_2137)", T, "23"),
    ("the separate model's golden edge-time join (2 Nov, filed 1 Nov 21:19)", "near/far cycles, Q6/H6 with H6^2 = 5I, R on the fixed plane, v- = N + phi^3 F, reflector (5, 1) det -125, doubling D with D R D^-1 = -R, marked moments", "replayed (notes_2137); R is the model's own Curl on the rotor plane (new identification); the marked-moment contract is recorded", T, "23"),
    ("the root-site compression (separate model's master model, 2 Nov)", "P_R H P_R = 240 I - B_R, B_R spectrum 56^1 28^8 8^35 (-2)^112 (-4)^84; compressed means 184, 212, 232, 242, 244", "replayed exactly on the lattice: a root difference is a root exactly at inner product 1; the five sector projectors are integer polynomials in the inner product (master_readout)", T, "23"),
    ("the source-marked J15 (master model, 2 Nov)", "an isometry J15 of the 15 atoms into root sites with J15^T B_R J15 = 28 P3 + 8 (P0 + P8) and H_K = 10 I15 - (1/4) J15^T B_R J15 - 8 P0; the mark P0 is needed", "the repository has no such map: its own atom-to-root maps, the fibres over the atom weights and the six-site port's bond roots, give Tr J^T B_R J = 70 and 0 against 280. One was built from the glue (carrier sites for the vertices, twin duads for the edges, ker M quadratics for P0, two invariant quadratics for P8); it is a scaled map, integer readings times 1/(10 sqrt60), 1/(10 sqrt180), 1/sqrt2400000, 1/sqrt4800000 and 1/sqrt192, an exact isometry satisfying the identity (B_R J = J M checked directly), and it carries the tick when the twin is labelled in the tick's order; the vertex/edge orthogonality forced by P3 puts the edges' linear parts in the twin's span (the carrier duads fail; the twin frame within that span is a choice). The mark is needed: J^T B_R J is 8 on all of P0 + P8. The separate model's own J15 is not in the repository and may differ on the P8 block (two invariant quadratics, an O(2) choice): a selected reference", SR, "23"),
    ("N44's 45 channels (master model, 2 Nov)", "21 native directions plus 8 root-linear and 16 mixed A4 x A4': multiplicities (1, 8, 26, 6, 4), means (184, 212, 232, 242, 243), BB* = 2117 I1 + 967 I8 + 389 I26 + 127 I6 + 83 I4, rank 45, trace 21061, least 83; the dark mean 243 is no root-graph eigenvalue", "replayed on the lattice (H and H^2 between the 360 sites of the root shell and the dark orbit): the blocks are mutually orthogonal and the means and second moments are scalar on each, so BB* is exactly as stated; the four dark functions span N44's dark reader (replayed); the ten centred carrier quadratics span exactly N43's ten edge readings (alpha_i - alpha_j)^2 - 1/2 (notes_0101), and BB* is basis-free on each span; the 8 linear (the whole linear sector) and 16 mixed (A4 x A4') directions are fixed as subspaces by the A4 + A4' marking", T, "23"),
    ("the self-energy bounds (master model, 2 Nov)", "BB*/(s + 256) <= Sigma(s) <= BB*/s for s > 0, spec C in [0, 256]", "a general operator inequality; checked for J15 on the lattice with the band edge (BB* = 967 P3 + 389 (P0 + P8)) and exactly on the finite root-site instance at s = 1, where even BB^T/245 <= Sigma(1) <= BB^T/185", T, "23"),
    ("the Schur-completed reference action (master model, 2 Nov)", "K = H + eps I + J V J* with V = K_g + X - A15 - eps I has static Schur complement K_g, quadratic form <q, K_g q> + |C_eps^(1/2) h + C_eps^(-1/2) B* q|^2 >= 0, and leaves Y* K Q K Y and the Krylov spaces unchanged", "general identities, replayed exactly on a finite rational instance from the model's operators (H_R = 240 I - B_R, the atoms on the six-site port's 15 bond roots, K_g = H_K, eps = 1); Krylov equality checked to K_3", T, "23"),
    ("the Feshbach/Woodbury source law (master model, 2 Nov)", "S_K(z)^-1 - S_0(z)^-1 = V, G_K = G_0 - C V [I + S_0 V]^-1 C* (rank <= 15), Tr[G_K - G_0] = d/dz log det(I + V S_0(z))", "general identities, replayed exactly at z = 1 on the same finite instance (the difference has rank exactly 15); the last step is Jacobi's formula, with S_0' = -C^T C checked against the sector expansion", T, "23"),
    ("one model time (master model, 2 Nov)", "U_A, U_A' commuting order-5 rotations with principal skew logs; Omega = Omega_A + Omega_A', exp(Omega) = U_A U_A' = the tick; co-rotating field Phi'' + K Phi = 0 with conserved energy", "exact for spine_clock's r, r' and g (the logarithms are polynomials in r, r'; angles 2 pi/5, 4 pi/5); the co-rotating field is read as the clock acting on solutions of Phi'' + K Phi = 0 for a finite K commuting with it (K = H_K, the tick U15 on the atoms): solution and energy conservation exact; the note's own definition of the co-rotating field is not in the repository", T, "23"),
    ("timed observability and the response scaling (master model, 2 Nov)", "sigma_min F(delta) >= sqrt83 delta^2/2 - M^2 delta^4/24, optimum delta* = sqrt(6 sqrt83)/M with 249/(2 M^2), delta = 1/36 positive at M = 256; (kappa, tau) -> (a^2 kappa, a tau) keeps rho and the response; fingerprints 1 + b_j/a_j^2", "the optimum, its value and the positivity at M = 256, delta = 1/36 (sqrt83/2592 - 32/19683) are exact; the bound follows from 0 <= cos x - 1 + x^2/2 <= x^4/24 (checked) and the spectral theorem for our reading F(delta) = Y* cos(delta sqrt H) Q H Y (BB*)^(-1/2); the scaling and the five fingerprints (= m2/m1^2) are exact", gates.CONDITIONAL, "23"),
    ("the master model's counts (2 Nov)", "45 = 1 + 8 + 26 + 6 + 4; 67 = 45 + 21 + 1", "the arithmetic holds and 45 and 21 are the channel counts built here (21 = 1 + 10 + 6 + 4 native); the final 1 of 67 is not identified", T, "23"),
    ("the full unification, part 2 (1-2 Nov)", "close every input the seed can reach and replay every replayable recorded claim of the survey", "the Standard-Model frame derived from the carrier's A4 (charges and the root assignment move into the derivation: 60 derived, 9 inputs, 3 built from them), the nine-torus joined to E8 by THEOREM, the datum, literal and words split into a derived part and a recorded selection, and AIR_801 into a derived residue and external integers; 71 joins and 89 ledger rows from nine adversarially reviewed units", T, "23, 25"),
    ("the datum's frame (seed closure, 1 Nov)", "the 600 data of the datum's type (20 A4 roots x 30 norm-4 zero modes), all of energy 34 and alike in every D^2 sector; the reading's stabilizer in W(E8) is W(A4) x W(A4') (14400), acting as S5 with five free orbits of 120; W(E8) leaves 4 Gram classes of the bare root triples, 3 with time reversal", "replayed exactly (datum_frame): the type and the representative are the seed's; the orbit with <r, a><r, b> = -1 is a recorded selection, one of five; the 14400-element stabilizer is enumerated exactly from the 115200 Gram-preserving images of A4 + A4''s simple roots", T, "23"),
    ("the literal operands in the time clock's chart (seed closure, 1 Nov)", "WAS_native = Chi o commutator o Lambda^2 N_source; Chi's rows are the pentagon edges and the pentagram circulation; W_p = 2 F^T F; 480 integral W_p-charts in one orbit of S5 x Aut(W_p) (40); the bath's 20 symmetries leave two orbits of 240 separated by the apex sign; N_source is five K4 matching modes", "replayed exactly (literal_chart) on data/native_matrices_input.json: only the apex sign (the pentagram along R^2, not R^3) and the basis N_source stay the owner's", T, "23"),
    ("the words against the Coxeter frames (seed closure, 1 Nov)", "the clocks act on the 15 frames as AGL(1, Z/15) (120); the D3's centralizer is {1, 4, 7, 13}; 72 equivariant bijections in 18 classes of 4; the 6 <-> 9 flip has order 2 while the orbit-swapping centralizer elements have order 4", "replayed exactly (word_frames): the identification is one of 18 classes, a recorded selection; the digits are decimal data", T, "23"),
    ("AIR_801's residue and integers (seed closure, 1 Nov)", "mod 5 one of the 20 GL(2,5)-conjugates of -d, forced by the day (k = 1, 5); det 12402 != +-1; discriminant 968473 = 11 x 17 x 5179, narrow class number 4 (2744 reduced forms, 4 cycles), one class per genus; columns 180-degree digit rotations", "replayed exactly (air801_classes): the residue is derived, the integers are external", T, "23"),
    ("the Standard-Model split (unify's input 'charges', layer 24's 'unique up to W(E8)')", "the 3 + 2 split chooses the gauge group; once chosen the table is unique up to W(E8) (stated, not computed)", "derived from the carrier's A4 (sm_frame): T3 = alpha/2, colour = the orthogonal A2, Y = the commutant line, Q killing a site give 40 triples, one S5 x {+-1}-orbit; 24192 A4 subsystems, one W(E8)-orbit (5806080 chains = |W|/120); stabilizer S3 x W(A4') of order 720, so 967680 frames, one W(E8)-orbit; the table is a function of the frame; only the Levi type 3 + 2 (not 4 + 1) is recorded, and it carries no number", T, "23"),
    ("the nine-torus in the star (STAR_OBSTRUCTED)", "the nine-torus meets the seed only by an obstruction", "all nine squared frequencies are the band's critical values computed from E8's roots (torus_places), so E8 -- torus is a THEOREM join beside the obstruction, which only says that no periodic E8/mE8 carries 6800/27 and 4025/16; the hypercharge's point carries 251, Q's 243 and T3's 224 (sm_frame)", T, "23"),
    ("the carrier universe's onset (join_e8_cosmology, layer 7)", "w = (1 - 16 m^2)/(1 + 16 m^2); accelerating iff m^2 > 1/8", "that reading holds the datum's velocity fixed in physical time; read natively, as the calibration convention m = 1/tau has it (dpsi/dt = m v0), w0 = -15/17 and q0 = -14/17 - (3/17) Omega_Lambda for every G and m, accelerating whenever Lambda_cc >= 0; the readings agree exactly at m = 1 (native_onset, an added CONDITIONAL reading)", gates.CONDITIONAL, "23"),
    ("the external scales (calibration, product geometry, FLRW)", "M4, f, L and m free; no internal number binds physical time", "one positive real tau (m = 1/tau, cosmos_calibration) plus M4 and the dimensionless l = L/m, F0, F1, F2; at this order only G m^2 and Lambda/m^2 are observable (Jacobian rank 2 of 4), and at fixed field G the native onset depends on m only through Lambda_cc/m^2 (native_onset)", gates.CONDITIONAL, "23"),
    ("the sum-of-squares lock (U19.74; layer 8, idx 4)", "r^2 = 9/40 locked by a sum of squares on two copies of a 5-space; a positive collar floor up to 224", "the lock replayed exactly (band_closures): K^T K = (10/9) P on Lambda^2 ker M; in the canon's saved operands W_AS^T W_p W_AS = (320/9) Lambda^2 M P' and Q4 = (1/2) g^T W_p g = |F(a, b)|^2; (40/9) rho^2 - Q4 = (5/18)(|a|^2 - |b|^2)^2 + (10/9)(a.b)^2 + (10/9)|(I - P)(a ^ b)|^2 as a polynomial identity in both bases; Q4 <= (40/9) rho^2, attained on the tick's rotation planes; the collar floor is not replayed (the collar stays open)", T, "23"),
    ("eps > 100 off the infrared ball (layer 8, idx 6)", "eps > 100 on the alcove outside |k|^2 <= 6, by 7,523 computer-assisted pieces", "replayed (band_closures): the Taylor bound 30 s - (3/2) s^2 on 4.23 < s < 15.77 and 346 outward-rounded simplex pieces (mpmath interval trigonometry, band.Iv arithmetic), least bound 100.108; 37 further pieces lie in the Taylor window", T, "23"),
    ("the lambda = -12 families (layer 8, idx 7)", "Morse indices 7 and 8 at lambda = -12, corrections -16/3 vs -17/8; recurrence order 11", "the indices and corrections replayed exactly (band_closures): c1 = 54 (A8, index 8) and 31/2 (A7 + A1, index 7), kappa = (c1 + 10)/4 = 16 and 51/8, -kappa/3 = -16/3 and -17/8, the method checked by c1 = -2 at E8 and D8; the factor -1/3 is the record's convention, and the order-11 claim stays as layer 14 has it (an operator of order 16)", T, "23"),
    ("the Miller eighth-power recurrence (layer 16, idx 28)", "a bivariate Miller eighth-power recurrence produced the walk counts", "replayed (band_closures): Miller's rule for K(t, z)^8 over Q[z] with walkfast's D8 + half-spin split gives W_0..W_12 equal to data/walks90.json; the sibling's own recurrence text is not given", T, "23"),
    ("the root-line identities (layer 16, idx 30)", "Phi'' and Phi''' never vanish together on a root line; a uniform dispersive bound min(1, 3.65 t^(-9/4))", "the one-dimensional part replayed exactly (band_closures): Phi'' = 32c^2 + 224c - 16, Phi''' = -32 sqrt2 (2c + 7) sin th, max(|Phi''|, |Phi'''|) between 165 and 166 at its least; with the transverse Hessian (36 + 24 cos th) I_7, least 12 at the 224 saddle (twice frontier's 6); the 8-dimensional constant 3.65 is not replayed", T, "23"),
    ("the root-wedge Green scalar (idx 119, 123)", "the minimum-energy bath and its Green scalar; the sibling's rounded lower Green values", "the lower Galerkin chain replayed exactly through n = 4 (band_closures): l4 = 1109112767220222846448832/254887081433869159889497521 = 0.0043513887..., increasing, with decreasing residuals; the minimizing bath Delta^-1 T itself and the sibling's digits (not stored) are not", T, "23"),
    ("the N33 sector sheet (idx 125, 155)", "moments 1, 242, 58702, 14267058; a characteristic polynomial of degree 18 and a minimal one of degree 9; neither the contrast list nor the triangle port's", "replayed and joined (band_closures, rootgraph -> moments): the canon's square port's moments per unit norm, exactly (1/12, 1/2, 5/12) of the root graph's quadratic, cubic and quartic sector sequences, the only nonnegative mixture; square = (hexagon + octagon)/2 with the hexagon pure cubic and the octagon (1/6, 0, 5/6); the degree-18 and degree-9 polynomials (the sheet's operator is not opened) are not", T, "23"),
    ("the six golden petals' commutant (sibling; idx 59)", "the six golden petals: overlap 1/5, commutant 2", "replayed exactly (view_closures): on the cycles the six Sylow rotor planes have commutant span{P_cycle, Curl}, Curl^2 = 5 P_cycle, the golden field Q(sqrt5) through J_H = Curl/sqrt5; they generate the 18-dimensional centralizer of Curl, M3(Q(sqrt5)); the overlap F_i F_j F_i = F_i/5 was already checked in pair_frame", T, "23"),
    ("the Hodge degrees 31 and 41 and the heat spectrum (sibling; idx 60)", "Hodge degrees 31 and 41 (surface degree 31, Hodge defect 2 x 31 - 41 = 21) and the heat spectrum 0, 3, 6, 3 +- sqrt5", "replayed exactly (view_closures) on the repository's hemi-icosahedron (_surface_labels): sizes 31 and 41 (one or both triangle orbits), rank 30 each, Euler characteristics 1 and 11, 21 shared cells; spectrum x (x - 6)^10 (x - 3)^8 (x^2 - 6x + 4)^6 with L2 = 3I + S, |S| Petersen, S^3 = 5S and 3 +- sqrt5 = 2 phi^(+-2); both orbits give x^11 (x - 6)^30", T, "23"),
    ("the F4KDS1 identification of the six Sylow views with the synthematic totals (hub, historical; idx 87)", "the six Sylow views are the six synthematic totals", "replayed exactly (view_closures): each Sylow 5-group of the cone S5 fixes exactly one of the six totals; label -> total is a bijection, equivariant for all 120 permutations (exceptional action on the labels) and the only equivariant one of the 720; a total's stabilizer is the F20 of its label", T, "23"),
    ("the pair map's generic Jacobian rank (idx 90)", "the nonlinear pair map (a, b) -> F_AS(a, b) has generic Jacobian rank 6 away from the witness", "replayed exactly (view_closures): rank 6 at the witness, the five dark-plane pairs and ten fixed integer pairs, so generically (the image lies in the six cycles); at most 4 on every collinear pair, by the symbolic identity J(s u, t u) = [t W_u, -s W_u] with W_u u = 0, and exactly 4 at (u, 2u) and (h0, 0)", T, "23"),
    ("the F20 adapter family's four-map basis (idx 90)", "a four-map basis of the F20 adapters in which F_AS has coefficients (-1/5, 3/5, 2/5, -2/5)", "replayed (view_closures) in a basis of our own, read off agni_factor's L_out (the hub's literal basis is not in the repository): Hom_F20(Lambda^2 ker M, cycles) = 4 solved directly, B1..B4 F20-equivariant, independent and not S5-equivariant, and F_AS = -(1/5) B1 + (3/5) B2 + (2/5) B3 - (2/5) B4", T, "23"),
    ("the odd and dark infrared constants (inherited in the hub; idx 94)", "the odd port's infrared density C E^6/12960000 and the dark port's C E^7/8709120000, C = 1/(1536 pi^4 30^4)", "the leading mean squares are replayed exactly (view_closures): 1/480 on every unit cycle (odd port, cubic onset, the dipole vanishing on the cycles) and 1/10752 on the dark four (dark port, quartic onset, moment tensors vanishing in degrees 0 to 3), by Gaussian moments; the densities, and the odd heat tail t^-7/(22394880000000 pi^4) that matches triangle_port, follow in wedge_port's convention, conditional on the standard Fourier asymptotics", gates.CONDITIONAL, "23"),
    ("the two-shell populations at the source witness (idx 94)", "6264/5 on the root shell and 1836/5 on the norm-four shell", "replayed exactly (view_closures): with the Parseval coefficients of the six Sylow lines the pair bivector has cut part 0, bright population 6264/5 = (144/160) |F_AS(a, b)|^2 with |F_AS(a, b)|^2 = 1392 and dark population 1836/5, total |a ^ b|^2 = 1620; with the min-norm coefficients the bright image is F_AS(a, b) itself", T, "23"),
    ("the ten-position derivative's gains (idx 98)", "the gains 4/3, 20/3 and (10 -+ 2 sqrt5)/3", "replayed exactly (view_closures) at all five dark planes in their primitive bases: DF DF^T has characteristic polynomial x^4 (x - 20/3)(x - 4/3)((x - 10/3)^2 - 20/9)^2; the gains depend on the plane's basis (an orthogonal basis of norms 4 and 3 gives 10/3, 8/3, (19 -+ sqrt41)/6)", T, "23"),
    ("the N33 six-view frame (hub, 09:54: J09; idx 161)", "six rank-four K_i on Lambda^2 P5 with sum (12/5) I10 and four-view spectrum (12/5)^3 (8/5)^3 (6/5)^3 (2/5); source-reported, the projectors not stored", "built from the model's six F20 mixers and replayed exactly (view_closures): K_i is the orthogonal projector onto the graph of c X_i, the sum is scalar only at c = sqrt6/2 (c > 0), where it is (12/5) I_10, tr K_i K_j = 28/25, every one of the 15 four-view sums has spectrum (12/5)^3 (8/5)^3 (6/5)^3 (2/5) (one to six views all computed); c = 1 is fusion_frame's 2 P_B + 3 P_D", T, "23"),
    ("N34-006: the six-view frame's condition number (canon N34; idx 162)", "the six-view analysis map has condition number sqrt6", "replayed exactly (view_closures), read as the four-view (two views erased) condition: any four views have frame bounds 2/5 and 12/5 on the ten, so condition sqrt((12/5)/(2/5)) = sqrt6; the full six-view frame is tight (condition 1) and five views give sqrt(12/7); the other 31 N34 claims are not touched", T, "23"),
    ("the [12, 6, 6] word code and the 924-case census (hub; layer 23, idx 96 and 108)", "a [12, 6, 6] word code with distances 1, 2, 5 over F2, F3, F5; a 924-case word census", "replayed exactly (code_closures) on the inferred generator [I6; S T] (the hub's generator is not stored): all four distances hold, with S T = 0 mod 2 and 2J mod 3; the census of the 924 six-sets gives 854, 782, 37 and 1 information sets over Q, F5, F3 and F2, but the hub's census values are not recorded, so nothing is compared", T, "23"),
